> until you hit {luu}, and then I guess you'd have to backtrack.
> Or is there some quirk of the grammar of LUhU that says it's not
> elidable before a sumti connective, so that if you want [lua dy] then
> you'd have to say:
> 
>    by e lua dy luu e gy

Essentially yes.  Because LAhE/LUhU form parentheses that enclose a full
sumti, any connectives will be heard as belonging to the enclosed sumti.

> ? And the terminators are not elidable in
> 
>    by e lua lae dy luu e gy luu ne zy

Right.

